<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nero</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">37–68 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a> · Also known as Nero Claudius Caesar Augustus Germanicus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nero was Roman emperor from 54 to 68 CE, the last of the Julio-Claudian dynasty, adopted heir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claudius">Claudius</a>. His reign saw the revolt of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boudica">Boudica</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, the settlement with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/parthia">Parthia</a> that placed Tiridates on the Armenian throne, the Great Fire of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in 64 and the persecution of Christians. Revolts by provincial governors led to his fall, and he took his own life in 68.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nero.jpg" alt="Nero" width="320" height="435" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nero_Glyptothek_Munich_321.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
